
label opening:

    scene black

    pause 1.0


    # --------------------------------------------------------------
    # Dandelion Field
    # --------------------------------------------------------------

    play music curtain_fall

    scene bg sky at old_bg
    with Dissolve(3.0)

    pause 1.0

    narrator "The field was dotted with the yellow heads of dandelions as far as the eye could stretch."

    narrator "They bristled back and forth gently in the warm breeze, almost begging for someone to pick them."

    narrator "Technically, dandelions are weeds. Flowers meant to be ripped out of the ground and tossed in a trash bucket."

    narrator "There's nothing pretty about them, and they just exist to be weeded and thrown out."

    narrator "Either way, here in this field, under this slice of clear Summer sky... they looked beautiful."

    narrator "Or maybe it wasn't the dandelions at all."

    narrator "In the middle of the golden-colored field was a beautiful girl in a white dress, dancing in circles."

    narrator "The flowers danced around her in the breeze, and the straw hat covering her head fell off."

    narrator "Her hair was fair, a shade or two darker than the dandelions around her."

    narrator "She let it fall over her shoulders and brush against the middle of her back, and sucked in a deep breath of the sweet Summer air."

    narrator "Then she picked up her hat, and held it."

    narrator "She didn't put it back on her head right away."

    narrator "Instead the dandelion girl grinned and held her hand over her eyes, looking at the bright blue sky overhead, and simply took it all in."

    narrator "It was something poetic."

    narrator "The kind of thing you'd expect someone to describe in a sonnet."

    narrator "Or maybe it was something you'd expect to find in a leisurely oil painting, something warm and comfortable to hang on your wall and gaze at when the temperature gets too cold outdoors."

    narrator "Mark watched the girl and felt a strange and somewhat painful deja vu, as though it was a scene he'd witnessed a dozen times before."

    narrator "Of course, that was absurd."

    narrator "It was their first meeting, and never before in his life had he met such a beautiful girl."

    narrator "But he watched her, and felt a feeling of... connection."

    narrator "Surely, somehow and somewhere, he had been in this field at this time."

    narrator "Was something like that possible?"


